{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip was a scheduled 21:15 pickup and the driver was still not there when the rider cancelled at 21:23:15. The trip record fixes the no-show deadline at 2026-08-19T21:20:00+08:00 and reports arrived_by_deadline = false with arrived_at null. Under POL-NS-24 the rider was therefore entitled to cancel at no charge from 21:20 onwards, and the 5.00 SGD charged to her must be refunded in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.driver_deadline.arrived_by_deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS evidence independently confirms the driver never reached the pickup. The arrival check reports corroborated = false, arrived_at = null and nearest_fix = null against an arrival radius of 50 m for a STANDARD pickup zone, so no fix places the driver within the POL-NS-21 arrival radius at any point in the trace; the driver's actual position after 21:09:30 was not at the pickup. The driver-no-show condition in POL-NS-24 is thus established on both the trip record and the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05056", "EV-TRIP-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check.corroborated",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver stopped and stayed stopped through the whole of the scheduled time and the free-wait window. The last moving fix reports 11 kph at 21:09:00; each of the 28 fixes from 21:09:30 to 21:23:00 reports 0 kph, and the trace covers only 1.697 km in total. Nothing in the trace shows a final approach to the pickup between 21:09:30 and the rider's cancellation at 21:23:15. Because arrived_at is null, the POL-NS-21 free wait never even began to run for this driver — there was no arrival from which it could start.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05056", "EV-TRIP-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver made no contact with the rider at all before the trip was cancelled. The trip record's contact_before_cancel block reports message_count = 0 and call_count = 0, with obligation_met = false; the chat log holds only the rider's two messages ('Hi, where are you? App shows you not moving' at 21:16:40 and 'Hello??' at 21:19:30); and the only in-app call in the record is the rider's own at 21:20:10, which the driver did not answer. Both limbs of POL-NS-23 fail. The rider cancelled only because the driver never appeared and never responded to her — the very situation that clause protects against — so the fee is voided with no driver compensation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05056", "EV-CHAT-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the driver not only failed to arrive but also failed to attempt any contact, POL-NS-24's second limb applies on top of the refund: a 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is due to the rider. The fare ledger's money block carries goodwill_credit_sgd at 5.00. Under POL-GEN-03 that credit is a referral naming the clause, not an escalation, and it does not suppress the monetary outcome.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05056", "EV-CHAT-05056", "EV-TRIP-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.goodwill_credit_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only account is 'Passenger cancel herself, why she complain. I was coming.' Nothing on this record supports it as a delayed approach. The traffic-data artifact for this trip, EV-ADVIS-05056-01, is MISSING: its admissibility status is MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, so it carries no fact and there is no advisory to explain any delay, whether inside or outside the free-wait window. The absence is citable and it counts against the driver, not the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05056-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-GEN-25"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money is straightforward and unmoved: the ledger shows cancellation_fee 5.00, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, while the derived money block sets fee_charged_sgd and refund_if_voided_sgd both at 5.00. A ruling that voids the fee therefore moves exactly 5.00 SGD back to the filing rider — a FULL_REFUND as POL-GEN-03 defines it, with driver_compensation_sgd null because POL-NS-23 voids the fee 'with no driver compensation'.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.refund_if_voided_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is nothing here for a human reviewer to resolve. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD threshold, and neither profile carries a fraud flag of 1 or more (both are 0), so the AI ruling is final at any confidence under POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26. Every fact POL-NS-24 and POL-NS-23 need — the deadline, the non-arrival, the absence of contact — is established on complete, weight-1.0 artifacts, so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged and the case should be decided on the merits in the rider's favour rather than held.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05056", "EV-DPROF-05056", "EV-TRIP-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-24: 5.00 SGD goodwill credit to the rider, because the driver failed to arrive at the pickup by the scheduled time plus 5 minutes and also failed to attempt any contact with the rider before the cancellation."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver, this is what the record shows and how the policy applies to it.\n\nThe booking was a scheduled 21:15 pickup. The driver's own device trace runs from 20:59:00 to 21:23:00, 49 fixes at 30-second spacing, full coverage and no gaps. It shows the car moving towards the pickup and then stopping at roughly 1.6 km from it: from 21:09:30 to 21:23:00 every one of 28 consecutive fixes reports 0 km/h, and the last fix is 15 seconds before the rider cancelled at 21:23:15. The platform trip record logs no arrival event at all (arrived_at is null), and its own deadline check reports arrived_by_deadline = false against a 21:20:00 deadline, which is the scheduled 21:15 plus the 5-minute free wait. The driver sent no chat message and placed no in-app call; the chat log holds only the rider's two messages (21:16:40 and 21:19:30, both read and unanswered) and the only call in the record is the rider's own at 21:20:10, which the driver did not answer.\n\nPOL-NS-24 (driver no-show) is the governing clause. Where the driver fails to arrive at the pickup by the scheduled time plus 5 minutes, the rider may cancel at no charge and any fee charged is refunded in full. The driver did not arrive by 21:20:00; the rider cancelled at 21:23:15, after the deadline. The 5.00 SGD on the fare ledger (cancellation_fee 5.00, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the derived money block's fee_charged_sgd and refund_if_voided_sgd both 5.00) is therefore refunded to the rider. That is a FULL_REFUND of the 5.00 SGD contested, and it is the whole contested amount.\n\nOn the driver's arguments. (1) The fee is exactly the policy figure: fee_charged_sgd 5.00 and policy_fee_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy true, so there is no amount error and no POL-NS-22 referral for a non-5.00 fee — that part of your position is right, but it speaks only to the size of the charge, not to whether it is owed. (2) Your point about POL-NS-23 is correct as far as it goes: that clause imposes the chat-and-call duty on a driver who cancels for no-show, and here it was the rider who cancelled, so POL-NS-23 does not by itself void the fee. It does not follow that the fee stands — POL-NS-22 only transfers the 5.00 SGD to the driver where the driver cancels after the free wait, and this driver neither arrived nor cancelled. (3) The submission that the arrival fact is unestablished (POL-GEN-26) is not accepted. Non-arrival is carried by two unimpaired weight-1.0 artifacts: the platform trip record (no arrival event, arrived_by_deadline false) and your own GPS trace (car stationary 1.6 km from the pickup across the whole window). Nothing the rule needs is missing, so the case is decided on the merits and not escalated. (4) Your continuous trace and the time spent driving are accepted as facts, but this category gives a driver compensation only on a driver-cancellation after the free wait, which did not happen; there is no entitlement here. (5) The missing traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-05056-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and carries no fact (POL-GEN-02); it does not establish or defeat anything, and it is not a reason to escalate. The driver's written account ('I was coming') sits against his own trace of a stationary car and is not relied on.\n\nOn the goodwill credit: POL-NS-24's second limb applies because the driver not only failed to arrive but also failed to attempt any contact at all before the cancellation. The rider is due a 5.00 SGD goodwill credit, which I record as a referral naming POL-NS-24. As POL-GEN-03 provides, that referral rides with the money ruling and does not replace it.\n\nOn who decides and what confidence: the contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD threshold, and neither party carries a fraud flag, so under POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final at any confidence. The deciding facts rest on artifacts of weight 1.0 (trip record, GPS trace, chat log), so my confidence is not capped below that. No repeat no-show referral under POL-NS-25 arises: the fee does not stand, and the profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d count. No driver compensation is payable on this ruling."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
